{"format":1,"seq":285,"writes":[{"type":"entry","value":{"model":[{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"With limited time left, I'm prioritizing four PRs by value and simplicity: first, fixing the CI workflow to add a proper node setup and dependency install before running the pi-action; second, hardening the project's helper functions by using safer npx invocation, checking node_modules exists beforehand, clamping wait timeouts, and preventing delivery commits from pushing to a protected default branch.\n\nI'm considering reworking the gh.api global to raise on truncated JSON and support an options object with method/fields/jq plus helpful error hints when members are missing, alongside npm.ci and git.switch/fetch/pull globals that would require regenerating the contract typings. Given the time budget, I'll likely only get through the CI fix and the project functions work, maybe touching the gh globals, so I'm starting now with the CI workflow by checking its current checkout step and figuring out how to add node setup consistent with the existing ci.yml pattern.\n\n","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_bdrk_01JhKeVVWkN2brEvs1j6bLv5","name":"typescript","arguments":{"code":"// @pit: {\"label\": \"Record plan note and inspect ci.yml node setup\"}\nasync ({ session: { setNote }, shell: { execFile }, runtime: { status } }) => {\n  await setNote(\"plan379\", \"PRs by area: A ci workflow npm ci; B project fns (.pi/functions: npx --no-install+preflight, wait clamp, commit protected); C gh globals (api truncation/options, missing-member hint); D npm.ci/git globals. Analysis data /tmp/calls.json\");\n  const r = await execFile(\"grep\", [\"-n\", \"-B2\", \"-A6\", \"setup-node\", \".github/workflows/ci.yml\"]);\n  return { r: r.stdout.slice(0, 2000), st: await status() };\n}"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"nvidia","model":"aws/anthropic/bedrock-claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":704,"cacheRead":63376,"cacheWrit